{"id":"8a5419e2086c0add","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-df-density.md","title":"Density","display":"df-density — Density","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-density","aliases":["58-df-density","Density"],"display":"df-density — Density","depends_on":["[[58-df-measure]]","[[../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]]","[[../batch03/58-df-ball.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-density"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-density</span><span>Density</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-density — Density"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"58-df-measure\">58-df-measure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"83a15c7e9b3817dc\" href=\"?note=83a15c7e9b3817dc\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"c0dd9ffea872a14a\" href=\"?note=c0dd9ffea872a14a\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-ball.md\">../batch03/58-df-ball.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L,E,x,X,d,\\mathcal M,\\mu\\in V\">\\(L,E,x,X,d,\\mathcal M,\\mu\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S\\)</span> (measure-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"83a15c7e9b3817dc\" href=\"?note=83a15c7e9b3817dc\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\\)</span> (metric-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B_d(x,r)\">\\(B_d(x,r)\\)</span> (metric ball, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"c0dd9ffea872a14a\" href=\"?note=c0dd9ffea872a14a\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-ball.md\">../batch03/58-df-ball.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DensityValue}_S\\subseteq V^7\">\\(\\mathrm{DensityValue}_S\\subseteq V^7\\)</span> (density-value predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}density}\\vdash\\mathrm{DensityValue}_S(L,E,x,X,d,\\mathcal M,\\mu)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal M,\\mu)\\land E\\in\\mathcal M\\land x\\in X\\land L\\in[0,1]\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists\\delta\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall r\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\Bigl(r&lt;\\delta\\to B_d(x,r)\\in\\mathcal M\\land\\mu(B_d(x,r))&gt;0\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{48mm}\\land\\left|\\frac{\\mu(E\\cap B_d(x,r))}{\\mu(B_d(x,r))}-L\\right|&lt;\\varepsilon\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}density}\\vdash\\mathrm{DensityValue}_S(L,E,x,X,d,\\mathcal M,\\mu)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal M,\\mu)\\land E\\in\\mathcal M\\land x\\in X\\land L\\in[0,1]\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists\\delta\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall r\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\Bigl(r&lt;\\delta\\to B_d(x,r)\\in\\mathcal M\\land\\mu(B_d(x,r))&gt;0\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{48mm}\\land\\left|\\frac{\\mu(E\\cap B_d(x,r))}{\\mu(B_d(x,r))}-L\\right|&lt;\\varepsilon\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The limit is expanded by an <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varepsilon\">\\(\\varepsilon\\)</span>-<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta\">\\(\\delta\\)</span> clause, and every sufficiently small ball is required to be measurable with positive measure before the quotient is formed.</li>\n<li>Lebesgue density: proportion of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E\">\\(E\\)</span> in small balls around <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\">\\(x\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Points of density 1: where <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\">\\(x\\)</span> is &quot;inside&quot; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E\">\\(E\\)</span> by measure-theoretic sense</li>\n<li>The almost-everywhere density statements are differentiation theorems, not part of the definition.</li>\n<li>Approximate density: asymptotic density in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{N}\">\\(\\mathbb{N}\\)</span>; arithmetic applications</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Mattila, Geometry of Sets and Measures in Euclidean Spaces</li>\n<li>Rudin, Real and Complex Analysis</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-measure","status":"resolved","id":"ca832ed6bc22f728","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-measure]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"83a15c7e9b3817dc","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch03/58-df-ball.md","status":"resolved","id":"c0dd9ffea872a14a","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-df-ball.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"83a15c7e9b3817dc","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S$ (measure-space predicate, see [[../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S$ (metric-space predicate, see [[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch03/58-df-ball.md","status":"resolved","id":"c0dd9ffea872a14a","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$B_d(x,r)$ (metric ball, see [[../batch03/58-df-ball.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"L,E,x,X,d,\\mathcal M,\\mu\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S","display":false},{"tex":"B_d(x,r)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DensityValue}_S\\subseteq V^7","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}density}\\vdash\\mathrm{DensityValue}_S(L,E,x,X,d,\\mathcal M,\\mu)\\leftrightarrow{}&\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal M,\\mu)\\land E\\in\\mathcal M\\land x\\in X\\land L\\in[0,1]\\\\\n&\\land\\forall\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\exists\\delta\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\forall r\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\Bigl(r<\\delta\\to B_d(x,r)\\in\\mathcal M\\land\\mu(B_d(x,r))>0\\\\\n&\\hspace{48mm}\\land\\left|\\frac{\\mu(E\\cap B_d(x,r))}{\\mu(B_d(x,r))}-L\\right|<\\varepsilon\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\varepsilon","display":false},{"tex":"\\delta","display":false},{"tex":"E","display":false},{"tex":"x","display":false},{"tex":"x","display":false},{"tex":"E","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb{N}","display":false}],"bytes":1881,"backlinks":[{"id":"b225c0aad9789a30","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$d(A)=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{|A\\cap(n+1)|}{n+1}$ (asymptotic density, see [[58-df-density]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-413","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-density.md|58-df-density]]（batch13）"}],"outgoing":["ca832ed6bc22f728","83a15c7e9b3817dc","ce876585d129ce97","c0dd9ffea872a14a"]}